        "content": "# Module 2 - Complete Notes\n```flowchart-text\nModule 2 — Variables & Data Types\n\nModule Flow Variables & Data Types\n  ↓\nData Types\n  ↓\nPrimitive Types\n  ↓\nVariables\n  ↓\nLiterals\n  ↓\nType Casting\n  ↓\nConstants\n  ↓\nNaming Rules\n  ↓\nPractice\n```\n## What is a Variable? A variable is a named memory location used to store a value. 📝 **Example**\n>\nint age = 20; Here: int → data type age → variable name 20 → value Think: age ↓ ```text\n┌─────────┐\n``` │ 20 │ ```text\n└─────────┘\n``` The value stored in a variable can generally be changed. int age = 20; age = 21; Now: age → 21 ## Data Types A data type tells Java what kind of value a variable can store. Java data types are broadly divided into: Data Types ↓ ```text\n┌────────┴────────┐\n``` ↓ ↓ Primitive Reference Primitive types Java has 8 primitive data types : byte short int long float double char boolean Reference types Examples: String Arrays Classes Objects Interfaces ## Primitive Data Types ⭐⭐⭐ Type Typical Size Example byte 8-bit 100 short 16-bit 20000 int 32-bit 100000 long 64-bit 100000L float 32-bit 10.5f double 64-bit 10.5 char 16-bit 'A' boolean JVM-dependent true / false Easy grouping Integer ↓ byte short int long Decimal ↓ float double Character ↓ char True / False ↓ boolean ## Integer & Decimal Types byte Stores small integer values. byte age = 20; Range:\n-128 to 127 short short marks = 500;\nRange:\n-32,768 to 32,767 int ⭐⭐⭐\nThe most commonly used integer type. int salary = 30000; Range:\n-2,147,483,648 to 2,147,483,647 long Used for larger integer values.\nlong population = 1400000000L; Use L when needed to make the literal a long. float Used for decimal values with single precision. float price = 99.5f; Use f/F. double ⭐⭐⭐ Used for decimal values with double precision. double salary = 45000.75; For most general-purpose decimal calculations, double is preferred over float. ## char and boolean char Stores a single character. char grade = 'A'; Use single quotes : 'A' 'B' '7' '$' Not: char grade = \"A\"; //\n- Double quotes represent a String.\nboolean Stores only: true false Example: boolean isPassed = true; Another example: boolean isLoggedIn = false; ## Variable Declaration & Initialization Declaration int age; The variable is declared but no value is assigned yet. Initialization age = 20; Declaration + initialization int age = 20; Flow: Declare ↓ int age ↓ Initialize ↓ age = 20 Multiple variables: int a = 10; int b = 20; int c = 30; You can also write: int a = 10, b = 20, c = 30; ## Literals A literal is a fixed value written directly in the program.\nExamples: int age = 20; 20 → integer literal double price = 99.5; 99.5 → floating-point literal char grade = 'A';\n'A' → character literal boolean passed = true; true → boolean literal String name = \"Prasanna\"; \"Prasanna\" → String literal. ## Type Casting ⭐⭐⭐ Type casting means converting a value from one data type to another. There are two important cases: Type Conversion ↓ ```text\n┌─────┴─────┐\n``` ↓ ↓ Widening Narrowing Widening Casting Smaller compatible numeric type → larger type. int x = 10; double y = x; Flow: int ↓ double Java can perform this automatically. 📝 **Example**\n>\n```java\nint number = 100;\ndouble value = number;\nSystem.out.println(value);\n```\nOutput:\n\n## 100.0 Narrowing Casting Larger numeric type → smaller numeric type. It generally requires explicit casting. double price = 99.99; int value = (int) price; Output: 99 The fractional part is discarded. Flow: double ↓ (int) ↓ int ## Constants & Naming Rules Constants A constant is a variable whose value cannot be reassigned after initialization. Use: final Example: final double PI = 3.14159; This is invalid: PI = 4.5; //\n- Common convention:\nMAX_VALUE MIN_VALUE PI COLLEGE_CODE Variable Naming Rules Valid int age; int studentAge; int age2; int _count; int $value; Invalid int 2age; //\n- starts with digit int student-age; //\n- '-' is not allowed int class; //\n- keyword Naming convention Use camelCase for variables: studentName totalMarks accountBalance Use PascalCase for classes:\nStudent BankAccount EmployeeDetails ## Important Programs + Revision Program 1: Student Details\n\n```java\nclass Student {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        String name = \"Prasanna\";\n        int age = 20;\n        double marks = 85.5;\n        char grade = 'A';\n        boolean passed = true;\n        System.out.println(\"Name: \" + name);\n        System.out.println(\"Age: \" + age);\n        System.out.println(\"Marks: \" + marks);\n        System.out.println(\"Grade: \" + grade);\n        System.out.println(\"Passed: \" + passed);\n    }\n}\n```\nOutput: Name: Prasanna Age: 20 Marks:\n\n## 85.5 Grade: A",
